{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/SwiftUI","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Testing","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Contexts","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Debugging","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Chains"],"title":"Development and Testing","generated":true,"anchor":"Development-and-Testing"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/factorykit\/previews"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mocking dependencies for SwiftUI Previews."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"FactoryKit"}],"title":"SwiftUI Previews"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Previews","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Factory can make SwiftUI Previews easier when we’re using View Models and those view models depend on internal dependencies. Let’s take a look."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"SwiftUI Previews","anchor":"SwiftUI-Previews","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here’s an example of updating a view model’s service dependency in order to setup a particular state for  preview."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ the view model","class ContentViewModel: ObservableObject {","    @Injected(\\.myService) private var service","    ...","    func load() async {","        let results = await service.load()","        ...","    }","}","","\/\/ the view","struct ContentView: View {","    @StateObject var viewModel = ContentViewModel()","    var body: some View {","        ...","    }","}","","\/\/ the preview","struct ContentView_Previews: PreviewProvider {","    static var previews: some View {","        ContentView()","            .withContainer(\\.myService) { MockService() }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If we can control where and how the view model gets its data then we can put the view model into pretty much any state we choose."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"SwiftUI #Previews","anchor":"SwiftUI-Previews","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The same can be done using the new macro-based #Preview option added to Xcode 15."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["#Preview {","    ContentView()","        .withContainer(\\.myService) { MockService() }","}"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Multiple Registrations","anchor":"Multiple-Registrations","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"There’s also a variant for Containers if you need to do multiple registrations.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["#Preview {","    ContentView()","        .withContainer {","            $0.myService.register { MockService() }","            $0.analytics.register { MockAnalytics() }","        }","}"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Multiple Previews","anchor":"Multiple-Previews","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If we want to do multiple previews at once, each with different data, we simply need to instantiate our view models and pass them into the view as parameters."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Prior to Xcode 15 and given the ContentView we used above, we’d need to do:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct ContentView_Previews: PreviewProvider {","    static var previews: some View {","        Group {","            Container.shared.myService { MockServiceN(4) }","            let vm1 = ContentViewModel()","            ContentView(viewModel: vm1)","            ","            Container.shared.myService { MockServiceN(8) }","            let vm2 = ContentViewModel()","            ContentView(viewModel: vm2)","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note the deprecated registration syntax."}],"type":"emphasis"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Of course, it’s even easier with #Preview as each one runs in its own context.."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["#Preview {","    ContentView()","        .withContainer(\\.myService) { MockServiceN(4) }","}","#Preview {","    ContentView()","        .withContainer(\\.myService) { MockServiceN(0) }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since the #Preview macro has been back-ported to iOS 13, there’s really no need to use the old syntax."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Common Setup","anchor":"Common-Setup","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If we have several mocks that we use all of the time in our previews or unit tests, we can also add a setup function to a given container to make this easier.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension Container {","    func setupMocks() {","        myService { MockServiceN(4) }","        sharedService { MockService2() }","    }","}","","#Preview {","    ContentView()","        .withContainer { $0.setupMocks() }","}"]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit"]]},"kind":"article","sections":[],"references":{"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Debugging":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/debugging","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Debugging","title":"Debugging","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Additional support for debugging resolution cycles, dependency chains and other issue.","type":"text"}]},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Contexts":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Changing injection results under special circumstances.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/contexts","title":"Contexts","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Contexts","kind":"article"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/SwiftUI":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Defining and using dependencies in SwiftUI.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/swiftui","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/SwiftUI","title":"SwiftUI","kind":"article"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Chains":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/chains","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Chains","title":"Circular Dependency Chains","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Detecting and solving Circular Dependency Chains.","type":"text"}]},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Testing":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Using Factory for Unit and UI Testing."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/testing","title":"Testing","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Testing","kind":"article"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A modern approach to Container-Based Dependency Injection for Swift and SwiftUI.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/factorykit","title":"FactoryKit","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit","kind":"symbol"}}}